WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.630
The three separated at a fork in the road.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:08.180
And now their whereabouts are undisclosed, do they want to protect themselves or other people.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.840
Or heavenly dreams?

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:12.770
The creases of disorder are a cauldron of three.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.470
To an endless, eternal picture of Hell,

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:19.510
pushing through time a door is dispelled.

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:24.700
Your grudge shall be released.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.690
Incidents like that are repeating in Tokyo.

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.950
Four victims already!

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:12.180
That’s… Come here.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.660
Oh, this one!

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:22.140
They say it’s just like what’s in this book.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.670
What? You don’t seem interested at all.

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.170
Akie, have you read that book?

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:32.850
I haven’t yet. I just saw it on the web.

00:01:32.850 --> 00:01:35.850
Well then, how do you know it’s true?

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:37.790
But… it’s probably true!

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.360
It’s scary!

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.870
Kamisaka-kun, did you bring what I asked for?

00:03:33.050 --> 00:03:33.730
Yes.

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:36.300
Here you go.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.580
Ah, thanks.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:43.360
Now my mother will be glad.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.140
It’s my first time knowing a novelist!

00:03:46.860 --> 00:03:49.100
Let’s continue being friends, eh?

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.540
Yes.

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:58.360
Reviews aren’t explosive, but still good.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:02.050
We’re thinking it can squeeze into the end of the year’s top ten.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:08.600
The reprinting and editing departments are really excited.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.590
Discussions about a movie are progressing, too.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.310
What happened to the incident?

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:17.600
Maybe it’s just coincidence.

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:23.060
Don’t anime and manga usually get criticized for things like that?

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.620
Novels are fine.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:27.640
Yea.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:31.090
Anyways, we hope you’ll write a new work.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:44.120
Because of the relation to the incident, the books sell, and the author gets famous.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.450
Probably leaked by the publisher as a publicity stunt.

00:04:50.630 --> 00:04:54.320
They’re not selling that well, and I’m not famous. Damn it!

00:04:58.950 --> 00:04:59.880
Yes?

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:02.250
Kamisaka Rokurou-san?

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:06.420
I am Asaba Sumi from the Weekly Reality Editing Department.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:07.660
It’s quite sudden…

00:05:13.590 --> 00:05:18.160
Its similarity to the novel, The Skyscraper’s Shadow, is quite a popular subject on the web!

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:21.970
The Skyscraper’s Shadow… don’t know it.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:28.380
Written by the rookie Kamisaka Rokurou, it won the Best Mystery award this year.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:32.000
It’s not a best-seller, but it’s being talked about a bit.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.640
And, what are you saying we should do?

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:38.640
I’ll go ask the author. I made an appointment with him last night.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:40.870
Well, do what you like.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:42.620
Yes.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:52.180
So, about the incident where the victim was forced to fall.

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:58.360
Some people said “publicity stunt,” which annoys me.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:04.050
Neither is the book selling because of the incident, nor am I now famous.

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:07.250
Everyone’s just guessing, I thought.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:15.160
But if the incident really was done because of your novel, any thoughts?

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:17.850
I would be angry.

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:21.810
Murderers kill because they want to, right?

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:26.810
I just wrote because I wanted to, and…

00:06:27.290 --> 00:06:30.520
What I’m saying may be a bit strange…

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:36.290
Some things can only be communicated aggressively or suspiciously!

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:42.930
I’m sorry, excuse me.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:44.940
Yes, this is Asaba.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:46.470
Yes?

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.370
What?! Really?!

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.410
The murderer has been caught!

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:53.280
What?

00:06:54.260 --> 00:06:57.870
Investigations on the arrested man continues.

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:04.950
Involved persons say he read a book, and did it because it was cool.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:10.140
The police are investigating based on the book’s influence on the incident.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:14.110
I will hold responsibility over summarizing your interview, Kamisaka-san.

00:07:14.110 --> 00:07:19.140
Be relieved, since I understand you’re not an irresponsible person.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.120
Thank you very much.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:27.580
Everything was fine until then…

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:35.980
Things I’d never said were printed.

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:41.540
As if I were against society. As if I had no common sense.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:47.930
I thought I was done for, trusting mass media.

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:49.880
See? Didn’t I tell you?

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:52.740
It’s related, see?

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:54.670
Isn’t it scary?

00:07:54.670 --> 00:07:58.120
Apparently this author lives in our city; did you know?

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:00.030
Really?

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:07.260
In the murderer’s home, the novel, The Skyscraper’s Shadow…

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:11.450
Horror films, and aggressive manga and games were found.

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:16.160
Seen as strongly influencing the murder, the police are still investigating.

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:20.450
The author, Kamisaka Rokurou-san…

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:22.270
Is he away?

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:25.260
As you can see, the curtains are shut, and the lights are off.

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:27.990
We could not talk to him.

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.390
Now the moment you’ve been waiting for.

00:08:30.390 --> 00:08:33.190
I can’t go home in this!

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:43.290
Shoboshi realized that dropping the girl from that fifty story building was his goal.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:46.160
Hime, it’s Moroboshi, not Shoboshi.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:49.050
How would I know that last name?

00:08:49.050 --> 00:08:49.440
Oh, Hime!

00:08:57.610 --> 00:09:02.260
What an unfortunate story! Even though he didn’t even kill her.

00:09:02.260 --> 00:09:07.180
It’s an unfortunate business. Aren’t writers all like that?

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:10.380
What is this?

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:14.910
It’s this: your manuscript was unusable.

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:19.430
And you replace it without permission? What happens to my trust?

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:22.940
Did you even establish trust?

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:29.140
Remember this if you’re a pro: it’s the result, how much it sells!

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:31.800
Are you saying you can change the truth just to sell?

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:36.800
Even if you don’t write truth, someone’s going to!

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:40.140
It just wasn’t your turn this time.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.720
<i>I did feel uneasy.</i>

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:51.780
What?! Even though I gave you this job!

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:55.610
<i>It was my fault for trusting the editor-in-chief too much.</i>

00:09:56.110 --> 00:10:03.370
I was thinking only about how to apologize to the unfortunate author.

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:08.150
The murderer’s name was Chouchi Hiroto.

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:10.840
Inori Public High School #3 2nd grade.

00:10:14.030 --> 00:10:15.370
Interesting…

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:42.200
What will I do with this 3 for Math?

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.930
Maybe I’ll tell my parents it’s out of 5.

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:48.950
But how will you explain 7 for Japanese?

00:10:48.950 --> 00:10:50.700
Cut it off and make it a one, maybe?

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:52.760
Then there’s no use!

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:54.250
Excuse me.

00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:58.720
I’m sorry, how can I get to town hall?

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:03.750
We’re going to the city to shop, so you can come with us.

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:04.740
I’m grateful.

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:11.460
Are you from Tokyo?

00:11:11.460 --> 00:11:12.150
Yes.

00:11:12.420 --> 00:11:14.800
Maybe a reporter?

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:15.250
What?

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:17.400
I’m sorry if I’m wrong!

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:22.160
Because of the incident, mass media people have increased tremendously.

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:25.000
No, it’s not that.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:27.950
I’m called Michio Yui.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:34.020
The first victim was my little sister.

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:34.900
What?

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:39.450
My little sister was the same age as the murderer.

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:45.490
I couldn’t believe a boy so young could do such a thing.

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:50.850
<i>So, I didn’t know who to hate.</i>

00:11:50.850 --> 00:11:55.880
<i>The direct murderer? Or the author?</i>

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:59.090
<i>I wanted to figure it out for myself.</i>

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:01.970
<i>The explicit murderer was…</i>

00:12:02.830 --> 00:12:07.900
<i>After reading that novel, I couldn’t tell reality from fiction.</i>

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:11.960
<i>So when I think of what I have done…</i>

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:16.050
<i>I don’t have any memory of it.</i>

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:22.470
<i>So I decided to meet that author.</i>

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:27.730
<i>And, if I figure out who to hate, I’ll…</i>

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:29.190
That’s the town hall right there.

00:12:33.180 --> 00:12:34.510
Thanks a lot.

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:35.500
Not at all!

00:12:37.410 --> 00:12:39.930
My mother said to give this back.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:45.800
If we had it, we would look bad, too.

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:50.690
Excuse me.

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.010
Oh, yes.

00:12:55.310 --> 00:12:57.590
I bet she’s another reporter,

00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:00.210
because you wrote such a weird novel.

00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:03.100
Really, what a nuisance!

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:10.990
Really, your little sister was…

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:13.870
So I wanted to figure it out.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:16.030
Who’s fault it really was.

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:20.610
I just wrote what I wanted to write.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.890
Then what’s this?

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:28.240
A fabrication of things I didn’t say.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:30.570
Where’s your evidence? You’re not just running away?

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:31.690
I have it.

00:13:39.100 --> 00:13:41.830
That kind of thing really happens, doesn’t it?

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:47.320
Yes, I was wondering how to make amends to Kamisaka-san.

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:50.540
But I realized I could only apologize face-to-face.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:56.560
That’s enough, please stop. I understand fully.

00:13:58.260 --> 00:14:02.070
Freelance writers are really powerless, aren’t they?

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:09.580
Looks like we’re in a horrible situation.

00:14:09.900 --> 00:14:14.530
Bad luck, I suppose, although it’s quite something that I should say.

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:19.800
I don’t want to make it luck’s fault! If possible, I want it crystal clear!

00:14:19.800 --> 00:14:26.330
The boy said if he made it the novel’s fault, his sentence would be less severe.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.030
Is that true?

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:32.560
He said that when bullying a classmate,

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:38.050
but is fearful of revenge, they refused to give testimony or their name.

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:42.590
If that’s true, then that guy was acting in front of me.

00:14:45.060 --> 00:14:52.570
I was planning to ask Jigoku Shoujo if I got a clear culprit.

00:14:52.590 --> 00:14:55.690
That I wanted them to go to Hell.

00:14:55.690 --> 00:14:57.090
Jigoku Shoujo?

00:14:57.090 --> 00:14:59.130
I’ve heard of her.

00:14:59.130 --> 00:15:04.470
At Midnight, if you submit someone’s name you hate to the Hell Correspondence site…

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:07.450
Jigoku Shoujo will ferry them to Hell.

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:14.800
But if you do, your soul will also go to Hell after death.

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:18.500
But even so, I thought it was OK,

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:23.320
since a life without my little sister was the same as it ending.

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:26.430
But if you send the murder to Hell,

00:15:26.430 --> 00:15:28.590
would that really be requittal?

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:31.990
Honestly, I don’t know.

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:36.010
I had the feeling that there was someone else to send.

00:15:37.720 --> 00:15:42.860
I got word from the publisher that the movie got canceled.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:48.730
We don’t even know if a new book can be published. The future looks grim.

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:52.020
So…

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:54.550
Well, um…

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:57.230
With us three…

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:01.550
We can send three people to Hell.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:21.020
I’ll pick the Editor-in-Chief, since the company probably couldn’t continue without him.

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:26.300
I wonder who I should pick?

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:34.050
Every person who insults me on the internet? Maybe that wouldn’t work.

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:37.750
Most likely, only one will work.

00:16:37.750 --> 00:16:42.850
Anyway, we two will do it, so maybe after you think about it thoroughly.

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:49.960
I thought of someone.

00:16:49.960 --> 00:16:54.910
Maybe not as serious as you two, but for me, I can’t forgive him.

00:17:08.300 --> 00:17:12.600
Even though nothing will change because of that.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:22.870
Shall we do it?

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:34.390
Kamisaka-san, are you sure about this?

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:35.380
Yes.

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:41.050
I think I, irresponsibly catering to this world, am most at fault.

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:43.210
I understand.

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:44.910
Well, on three, then.

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:47.080
One, two, three!

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:51.960
Your grudge is received.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:55.720
What’s this? What is going on here?

00:18:56.340 --> 00:19:00.240
Well, I think you’d understand without me saying a thing.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:18.440
Where is this?

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:20.170
What is going on?

00:19:25.290 --> 00:19:30.150
Aren’t journalists supposed to communicate the truth?

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:52.790
What… what is this?

00:19:53.020 --> 00:19:55.340
Mom, where is this?

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:59.280
Support him when good, stepping on him when bad for you.

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:02.800
He can’t forgive you.

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:05.040
What? Kamisaka?

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:07.750
That’s just what my mother told me!

00:20:08.450 --> 00:20:11.070
I have sympathy for him, really!

00:20:11.070 --> 00:20:13.870
So help me! Please!

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:17.350
Says he, Ojou.

00:20:31.360 --> 00:20:33.570
O pitiful shadow, wandering in darkness.

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:36.580
Scarring people and degrading them.

00:20:37.390 --> 00:20:40.050
The ball of Karma is drowned in sin.

00:20:43.820 --> 00:20:46.550
Do you want to die this once?

00:20:48.070 --> 00:20:52.620
What did I do and what am I going to be?!

00:21:09.210 --> 00:21:12.350
Those people too are in Hell by now.

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:16.940
This is a connection, so…

00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:19.920
Maybe we should get together occasionally and drink?

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:22.060
A Hell Meeting, maybe!

00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:26.320
Anyway, let’s drink a cup.

00:21:32.260 --> 00:21:37.130
It feels as though the wind is blowing a bit more freely in the world.

00:21:37.130 --> 00:21:38.740
But it doesn’t feel real yet.

00:21:41.040 --> 00:21:42.240
Kamisaka-san?

00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:55.150
What?

00:21:56.390 --> 00:21:57.940
This suddenly?

00:21:57.940 --> 00:22:00.300
Someone sent you to Hell.

00:22:03.910 --> 00:22:06.170
The murderer’s mother.

00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:10.670
She thinks it’s your fault he became like that.

00:22:10.670 --> 00:22:14.550
But… what happens by cursing me?

00:22:14.550 --> 00:22:17.900
The person you cursed said the same.

00:22:17.900 --> 00:22:19.150
I just…

00:22:19.660 --> 00:22:21.930
Wrote what I wanted to write!

00:22:21.930 --> 00:22:23.700
That was it!

00:22:23.700 --> 00:22:24.430
Hey!

00:22:28.800 --> 00:22:30.430
Note: Kikuri wants Furigana, it's what younger kids use to read Kanji in books.

00:22:28.880 --> 00:22:30.430
Write down how to read these words!

00:22:34.190 --> 00:22:38.980
This grudge will ferry you to Hell.

00:22:45.210 --> 00:22:49.020
I will release your grudge.

00:24:20.860 --> 00:24:22.540
Your name?

00:24:22.540 --> 00:24:24.010
Nomura Nobuo.

00:24:24.010 --> 00:24:26.730
Cursing a graph, eh?

00:24:26.730 --> 00:24:30.820
Just because it’s summer doesn’t mean you can do anything you want!

00:24:30.820 --> 00:24:33.050
Everyone annoys me!

00:24:33.050 --> 00:24:34.800
I’ll send you to Hell.

00:24:34.800 --> 00:24:36.700
But I only have one chance…

00:24:36.700 --> 00:24:40.000
Who will it be to fall to Hell?

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.580
You?! You?! Or is it you?!

00:24:43.250 --> 00:24:45.200
What’s up with this person?

00:24:45.690 --> 00:24:48.250
Next Time: Mid-Summer Graph.

00:24:50.790 --> 00:24:55.640
This program is made possible by Sony Music,

00:24:55.640 --> 00:24:59.020
and the listed sponsors.
